{"full":"hf:hanjian/GRN","spaceId":"hanjian/GRN","name":"Generative Refinement Networks","source":"huggingface","description":"Generative Refinement Networks","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":9,"created":"2026-04-16T03:30:51.000Z","updated":"2026-08-03T12:02:56.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://hanjian-grn.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/hanjian/GRN","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T06:57:55.821Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T06:57:55.821Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T06:57:55.821Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is the official implementation of the paper Generative Refinement Networks for Visual Synthesis. Neither diffusion nor autoregressive — GRN is a third way. 🧠 Refines globally like an artist. ⚡ Generates adaptively by complexity. 🏆 New SOTA across image & video. The visual generation paradigm just got rewritten.","Diffusion models dominate visual generation but they allocate uniform computational effort to samples with varying levels of complexity. Autoregressive (AR) models are complexity-aware, as evidenced by their variable likelihoods, but suffer from lossy tokenization and error accumulation.","We introduce Generative Refinement Networks (GRN), a new visual synthesis paradigm that addresses these issues:"],"features":["June 8, 2026: ✈️ The training & fine-tuning code for GRN-T2I and GRN-T2V is released.","June 3, 2026: 🍉 A toy image-video dataset is provided for GRN-T2I/GRN-T2V training and fine-tuning.","May 23, 2026: 🌺 We release the training and evaluation code for HBQ tokenizer, enjoy","April 14, 2026: 🤗 Paper and code release","Near-lossless tokenization via Hierarchical Binary Quantization (HBQ)"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/hanjian/GRN/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b9f66ec80cff65b40d13661ef46d1f50a69